      {
        "id": 147754,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-17T18:09:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is it correct that every piece of art on a SotM card originated in a Sentinels Comic (or would have originated in a Sentinels Comic if they actually existed?)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I believe the answer is totally yes here</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jan111\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ad7895/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jan111:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Shame that there is not more info for some of the artwork on the cards. Some make me really curious about what&nbsp;happened. On the other&nbsp;hand it makes the characters more interesting and makes me fantasise about what happened to them. So thats a really cool aspect of it. Plus the gameplay is great <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There is some solid info on a handful of incap sides, but not too many.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For instance, Wraith's incap in the graveyard. There is a point in the Freedom Five comics that it switches back to the Freedom Four for one issue, then back to Freedom Five (forget the serial numbers). It was during that point Wraith was thought to be dead (though the specifics of that storyline are anyones guess).</p>\n<p>You are not alone, trust me. There are so many incap art's that I'd love for Christopher/Adam to expand upon and talk about. But unless they ever get around to doing the Letters Page project, I doubt those story details will be made public anytime soon (if ever).</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
